Run the script once yourself, in a PowerShell session with the ActiveDirectory module and an account that may create users and change their account options. The account is the bait, not the file, and nobody learns its password: the script generates it and does not keep it. Then move the account to the organizational unit of your service accounts and keep the script where the documentation of the directory is, if you want it to be found. The script raises no event on its own; only a request for a ticket for the account `{{.Persona.LegacyAccount}}` without preauthentication does, and only on a domain controller whose log you forward.
